NEAR-01: Reassociate rate expressions around their invariant parts

BIT-04 caches the parts of an expression that depend only on parameters,
constants and hydraulics, but only where they form a left prefix, since
moving anything else changes the order of the operations. Reorder products
and sums so that those parts come first, and fold constants, so that more
of each expression is cached per pipe: Richmond's Kdet*Xa*U*Av becomes
(Kdet*U*Av)*Xa. Results change at the level of rounding.

Requires: none
Results: near (concentrations move at the level of rounding; see 2-near-identical/README.md)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, after FIX-01, FIX-02
and BIT-01 to BIT-17 (the other near-identical changes are not needed):
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn NEAR-01.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

